<title>JAPAN: Japan March corn imports rise 19.1 pct yr/yr - MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan March corn imports rise 19.1 pct yr/yr - MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's corn imports in March totalled 1,512,727 tonnes, up by 19.1 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Monday showed.</p>
<p>Details were as follows, in tonnes:</p>
<p>			  Mar 97	 Feb 97	  Mar 96</p>
<p> Total		1,512,727     1,175,293     1,270,140</p>
<p> Feed corn total    896,633	 781,178	 806,592</p>
<p> Others		 616,094	 394,115	 463,548</p>
<p>Top suppliers of feed corn (in tonnes):</p>
<p> U.S.		   896,633	 781,178	 806,592</p>
<p>Total feed corn imports during the first three months of calendar 1997 reached 2,547,827 tonnes against 2,415,725 tonnes a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodity Desk (+81-3 3432-7391)</p>
</text>
